WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.447
You have now moved from advanced query writing to reusable analytical design.

00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:13.562
In this module, you learned how standard views centralize live logic, how materialized views store snapshots,

00:00:13.562 --> 00:00:19.804
how dependencies affect change management, and why access and freshness need to be part of the design.

00:00:20.481 --> 00:00:27.713
Module 13 takes these same analytical habits into a distributed environment with Spark S Q L and Microsoft Fabric.

00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:34.443
The technology changes, but the important questions remain familiar.

00:00:34.443 --> 00:00:35.023
What does one row represent?

00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:38.958
Where does the data come from?

00:00:38.958 --> 00:00:44.818
How current is it? And how can we validate that the output still means what we think it means?
